      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "To analyze the factor structure and psychometric properties of the TFEQ in a morbid obese Spanish sample of bariatric surgery candidates."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "Multi-trait/ multi-item analyses and alpha coefficients were conducted to test the convergent /discriminant validity and the internal consistency reliability. Principal components analyses (varimax) were used to explore the factor structure. Sub-group factor analyses by gender, age and body mass index (BMI) were conducted to identify unstable items."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The internal structure of the original TFEQ factors was unsatisfactory, especially the Disinhibition Scale. Most Disinhibition and Hunger items were grouped on one factor labeled &ldquo;Dysregulation Eating&rdquo;. Cognitive Restraint was split into two factors. The first one, related to the behavioral component of Restraint, labeled &ldquo;Restrained Behaviour&rdquo; and the second one related to weight and eating concerns called &ldquo;Predisposition to Restraint&rdquo;."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The original factor structure of the TFEQ was not replicated. A revised 23-item instrument, representing the three new derived factors is offered as a valid screening instrument for severely obese patients."
        }
      ]},
